    {
      "record_id": "switch:locres:set-01:USDLevelSequenceHelper:VisibilityWarningTooltip:21ea7edb",
      "source": {
        "set": "set-02",
        "namespace": "USDLevelSequenceHelper",
        "key": "VisibilityWarningTooltip",
        "jp_record_id": "switch:locres:set-01:USDLevelSequenceHelper:VisibilityWarningTooltip:21ea7edb",
        "official_en_record_id": "switch:locres:set-01:USDLevelSequenceHelper:VisibilityWarningTooltip:21ea7edb",
        "jp_sha256": "761a64295f963b80c7394aa60cb0ba1026adaadb702fd6ea52c1d4e113d2064a",
        "official_en_sha256": "243c0504f14d0f54fe180689177b78cad055171638e9acca7c7ce2b5f9f3e5b3"
      },
      "text": {
        "jp": "USD の可視性が継承されます (親のプリミティブが非表示の場合に、その子も暗黙的に非表示)。一方 Unreal では継承されません。つまり、Unreal で可視性のアニメーションを制作すると、USD ステージで予期しない結果になることがあります。\n\n可能な場合に [File (ファイル)] > [Regenerate sequence (シーケンスを再生成)] によりレベルシーケンスとステージの最新ステートを再同期すると便利です",
        "official_en": "Visibility in USD is inherited (if a parent prim is hidden, its children are also implicitly hidden), while it is not inherited in Unreal. This means that authoring visibility animation from Unreal may have unexpected consequences on the USD stage.\n\nYou may want to use 'File -> Regenerate sequence' to resynchronize the LevelSequence with the current state of the stage, whenever is convenient.",
        "real_en": null
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "UNREVIEWED"
